Q: What is the best practice when an expression is required in signal forms [formField]? A: <p>Do not put expressions inside <code>[formField]</code>. <code>[formField]</code> expects a Signal Forms field, not the field value.</p>
<p>Wrong:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;input matInput [formField]=&quot;toDisplayString(formModel.myenum().value)&quot;/&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Correct:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;input matInput [formField]=&quot;form.myenumDisplayString&quot; /&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>In formModel</p>
<pre><code>interface MyFormModel {
    myenum: MyEnum;
    myenumDisplayString: string;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Mapper:</p>
<pre><code>dtoToFormModel(dto: MyDto): MyFormModel {
  return {
    myenum: dto.myenum,
    myenumDisplayString: toDisplayString(dto.myenum),
  };
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> if it is only for display, it's better to use a computed value and not use <code>[formField]</code></p>
